This is the exact, machine-generated API: both halves of it produced from the same
Zig declarations the library compiles, so neither can drift away from the code it
describes. For *which* surface to reach for and how to start, see
[Surfaces]($link.page('surfaces')); this page is the lookup.

## The Zig API

The [Zig API reference]($link.page('reference/api')) is generated from the public
`pancake` module on every site build. It is the exact surface a Zig consumer imports,
with the ownership and lifetime notes attached to the declarations that carry them.

## The C ABI

The C surface is
[`pancake.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake.h),
generated from the same Zig declarations, so the header and the library can never
silently disagree. The optional iroh transport adds
[`pancake_iroh.h`](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/include/pancake_iroh.h)
as a superset. For the route from a build to a first complete C program, read
[consuming pancake from C](https://codeberg.org/jimisaacs/pancake/src/branch/main/docs/consuming-from-c.md).
